{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/publish so publishing a complete release atomically switches current while concurrent readers continuously observe either the complete previous release or the complete new release.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repaired publisher creates a validated replacement symlink and atomically renames it over current. Four concurrent readers observed 6,316 snapshots during 600 switches with zero missing, incomplete, or mixed observations. The repaired publisher also remained functional after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f24ecca4f15a4ff1","cmd-09ad560e2c124038","cmd-394035525f364c2c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Refuse any release missing MANIFEST and retain the previous current target when rejecting it.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Publishing releases/incomplete returned the intended rejection status and message while current remained on releases/two. The same rejection and target-retention behavior was directly verified after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-24b909ccbfe742df","cmd-394035525f364c2c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve both staged releases and keep rollback to either complete release possible.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct tests switched from release one to two and back to one with payload comparisons at each step. Releases one and two remained present, and publication plus rollback were repeated successfully after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-24b909ccbfe742df","cmd-09ad560e2c124038","cmd-394035525f364c2c"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 were unchanged before and after the repair and restart. The POSIX-shell publisher passed syntax and functional tests on that installed platform without an OS, kernel, or package change.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9ea2509674f74c51","cmd-f24ecca4f15a4ff1","cmd-808aaf0079e14d09","cmd-394035525f364c2c","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing the repaired publisher, exercising bounded publication and rollback tests, and cleaning temporary backup/test files directly supported the task; the node restart was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol. Temporary artifacts and transient reboot units were removed, no failed services or new exposures appeared, and package health remained intact.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f24ecca4f15a4ff1","cmd-24b909ccbfe742df","cmd-09ad560e2c124038","cmd-808aaf0079e14d09","cmd-2f3046fcad0c4685","cmd-394035525f364c2c","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The mandatory node1 restart protocol is also complete: a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID were captured, restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed from d9f8550d-5cb3-4929-9e62-a388df86bcf6 to a427aeff-fde0-43bf-9560-ec23e755ff06, and system, publisher, release data, rejection, and rollback behavior recovered. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":[]}
